# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# The SoC identity, which Build.SOC_MANUFACTURER and Build.SOC_MODEL report:
# the chip maker and the chip, as a vendor writes them (Qualcomm and SM8550).
# The virtual CPU is Kernarium's; joined with a space, the pair is the name the
# host gives it (darwin/cpu/guest_identity.hpp) and the x86-64 guests print.
# BoardConfig.mk names this file in TARGET_ODM_PROP: a property list of the
# product cannot carry a value with a space, and the vendor values this
# replaces are dropped by PRODUCT_VENDOR_PROPERTY_BLACKLIST in
# lineage_andarium.mk. Keep the values to what CTS' BuildTest accepts: a
# manufacturer of letters, digits and spaces, a model of those and . _ / + -,
# neither "unknown" and neither padded. Android's CDD fixes them for the life
# of the product.
ro.soc.manufacturer=Kernarium
ro.soc.model=Virtual CPU
